Subject: hls: http(s) URLs with caller-supplied I/O and no http protocol

open_url() accepts a segment, key or init-section URL only when avio_find_protocol_name()
names http(s), file or data. A caller that opens every URL itself -- io_open on a context with
AVFMT_FLAG_CUSTOM_IO, as WebKit's media player on Phoenix does so that cookies, TLS, CORS and
the HTTP cache stay the browser's -- builds FFmpeg with --disable-network, so there is no http
protocol to name and every remote segment fails with AVERROR_INVALIDDATA before io_open is
reached. With custom I/O, name http:// and https:// URLs (also behind crypto+ / crypto:) by
their scheme instead; is_http then follows as for the http protocol (byte ranges travel as
the offset/end_offset options, no avio_seek). Nothing changes without AVFMT_FLAG_CUSTOM_IO.

LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -658,6 +658,19 @@
     if (!proto_name)
         proto_name = avio_find_protocol_name(url);
 
+    /* A caller that opens every URL itself (io_open with custom I/O, e.g. a web browser
+     * whose own loader fetches the bytes) needs no http protocol in this build: name
+     * http(s) URLs by their scheme then. */
+    if (!proto_name && (s->flags & AVFMT_FLAG_CUSTOM_IO)) {
+        const char *inner = url;
+        if (av_strstart(url, "crypto", NULL) && (url[6] == '+' || url[6] == ':'))
+            inner = url + 7;
+        if (av_strstart(inner, "https://", NULL))
+            proto_name = "https";
+        else if (av_strstart(inner, "http://", NULL))
+            proto_name = "http";
+    }
+
     if (!proto_name)
         return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
 
